you in person this time.

00:00:04.563 --> 00:00:05.527
- [Sam] Yes!

00:00:05.527 --> 00:00:06.599
- Yeah. That's hilarious.

00:00:06.599 --> 00:00:07.699
- Oh, thank you. I hope so.

00:00:07.699 --> 00:00:09.866
- Oh my gosh, it's so funny.

00:00:09.866 --> 00:00:11.236
So ha- have y'all ever met before, Jen?

00:00:11.236 --> 00:00:12.379
- No, it's our first time.

00:00:12.379 --> 00:00:14.087
- [Kelly] Okay, right on.
- It's nice to meet you.

00:00:14.087 --> 00:00:14.920
- That was hilarious.

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:15.753
- Thank you so much.

00:00:15.753 --> 00:00:17.428
- I'm like, just the one
clip and I'm in. Yeah.

00:00:17.428 --> 00:00:18.261
- Yeah.

00:00:18.261 --> 00:00:20.388
- But last time, I don't think
I got a chance to ask you

00:00:20.388 --> 00:00:22.441
how, like, how did you get
into like standup, in comedy?

00:00:22.441 --> 00:00:24.888
- Man, I started standup, I was 29.

00:00:24.888 --> 00:00:25.872
- [Kelly] Ah.

00:00:25.872 --> 00:00:28.327
- Just looking for direction, really.

00:00:28.327 --> 00:00:29.847
Just kind of feeling like I had a life

00:00:29.847 --> 00:00:32.022
with no purpose and I
always wanted to do it.

00:00:32.022 --> 00:00:33.306
So I was like, yo, just give it a shot.

00:00:33.306 --> 00:00:34.139
- Yeah.

00:00:34.139 --> 00:00:34.972
- And I went up

00:00:34.972 --> 00:00:37.199
and I did this open mic and I got booed

00:00:37.199 --> 00:00:38.032
(Crowd Chuckles)

00:00:38.032 --> 00:00:38.898
- [Jen] Oh, (beep).

00:00:38.898 --> 00:00:39.731
- Immediately

00:00:39.731 --> 00:00:41.397
- [Kelly] Wow.
- But the setup was bad.

00:00:41.397 --> 00:00:42.230
The setup was bad.

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:43.896
- Yeah.
- It was like at a bar

00:00:43.896 --> 00:00:45.102
and they were watching football
and then they like turned

00:00:45.102 --> 00:00:47.730
off the football and they were
like, it's comedy time y'all.

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:48.563
And

00:00:48.563 --> 00:00:49.396
- [Kelly] Oh

00:00:49.396 --> 00:00:50.650
- that already sets you
up for like failure.

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:52.275
- That was, that was Satan's work.

00:00:52.275 --> 00:00:53.151
- Yeah, right.

00:00:53.151 --> 00:00:54.453
- That was the devil's work.

00:00:54.453 --> 00:00:55.286
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:55.286 --> 00:00:56.339
- It wasn't the best position to be in.

00:00:56.339 --> 00:00:57.466
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh.

00:00:57.466 --> 00:00:58.408
- Pressure!

00:00:58.408 --> 00:00:59.676
- Drunk football fans.

00:00:59.676 --> 00:01:00.509
- Yeah.

00:01:00.509 --> 00:01:01.342
- Wow that was...

00:01:01.342 --> 00:01:02.175
- Yeah.

00:01:02.175 --> 00:01:03.042
- But you kept going.

00:01:03.042 --> 00:01:04.741
- Yeah, it was like, as
soon as I got on the mic too

00:01:04.741 --> 00:01:07.175
I was like, you ever, and
someone was like, boo!

00:01:07.175 --> 00:01:09.517
And I was like Aww (Jen and Crowd Laughs)

00:01:09.517 --> 00:01:10.500
- [Sam] Cool.

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:12.281
- Do you lean into a heckler?

00:01:12.281 --> 00:01:13.114
- Um That time?

00:01:13.114 --> 00:01:15.554
No. I was like, you know
what, I'm gonna just leave

00:01:15.554 --> 00:01:17.599
and let you guys do what you want to do.

00:01:17.599 --> 00:01:19.139
- Oh my God. Deuces.

00:01:19.139 --> 00:01:20.312
- But I wasn't discouraged,

00:01:20.312 --> 00:01:21.382
which is the most important thing.

00:01:21.382 --> 00:01:22.215
- That's what I'm saying.

00:01:22.215 --> 00:01:23.048
- Yes

00:01:23.048 --> 00:01:23.881
- You kept going. (Clapping)
That's incredible.

00:01:23.881 --> 00:01:24.714
- For sure.

00:01:24.714 --> 00:01:26.286
- And that's an incredible
story to tell people

00:01:26.286 --> 00:01:29.209
because everybody thinks it's
so easy when they see us here

00:01:29.209 --> 00:01:30.652
and it's like, there are a lot

00:01:30.652 --> 00:01:31.928
of doors that are shut

00:01:31.928 --> 00:01:34.443
and mean uh men usually
involved (Sam chuckles)

00:01:34.443 --> 00:01:36.385
but there is a lot of things
that happen that deter you.

00:01:36.385 --> 00:01:37.218
- Yes.

00:01:37.218 --> 00:01:38.884
- You know? So that's really
cool that you kept going.

00:01:38.884 --> 00:01:39.975
What a great story that is.

00:01:39.975 --> 00:01:40.962
- Yeah. Man, you got to

00:01:40.962 --> 00:01:43.098
or you won't get to where
you're trying to go, you know?

00:01:43.098 --> 00:01:44.914
- Amen. I get it. I get it.
- Yes, thick skin

00:01:44.914 --> 00:01:46.580
- What's your toughest moment
on stage? You ever been

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:47.413
- Ooh

00:01:47.413 --> 00:01:48.246
- like booed or any
kind of weird situation?

00:01:48.246 --> 00:01:50.050
- Yeah. Well, my very first time on stage

00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:54.174
was my first recital
performance. I fell like, I -

00:01:54.174 --> 00:01:58.279
we were bumblebees and I
fell and knocked all the

00:01:58.279 --> 00:02:00.612
other bumblebees down Kelly.

00:02:01.452 --> 00:02:03.367
like, like dominoes.

00:02:03.367 --> 00:02:05.508
They all just went down because of me.

00:02:05.508 --> 00:02:08.598
And so my very, the fact that
I kept with it and was like

00:02:08.598 --> 00:02:09.431
- Right

00:02:09.431 --> 00:02:10.264
you know

00:02:10.264 --> 00:02:12.491
I'm gonna keep doing this even
though I- I- failed miserably

00:02:12.491 --> 00:02:14.344
- Did they all turn on you?
Like behind, backstage?

00:02:14.344 --> 00:02:15.563
- I think we were too young.

00:02:15.563 --> 00:02:16.718
But, you know, few years later

00:02:16.718 --> 00:02:17.835
it probably would've been opposite

00:02:17.835 --> 00:02:18.746
- You were the goal

00:02:18.746 --> 00:02:19.959
- You were the bee that ruined it all

00:02:19.959 --> 00:02:21.625
- The Bee!
- And they're holding onto it.

00:02:21.625 --> 00:02:23.342
- But you know, you do the
thing afterwards where you

00:02:23.342 --> 00:02:25.023
uh uh uh yeah. That that was meant to be.

00:02:25.023 --> 00:02:25.963
That was meant to be.

00:02:25.963 --> 00:02:28.113
And they were like, oh, Jen, you fell.

00:02:28.113 --> 00:02:30.246
- I have fallen on stage, not as a kid.

00:02:30.246 --> 00:02:31.079
- For real?

00:02:31.079 --> 00:02:33.409
- Oh. Like full on over.

00:02:33.409 --> 00:02:34.894
I fell back, I think it was

00:02:34.894 --> 00:02:37.879
over Corey's board, like his
guitar, whatever you call that.

00:02:37.879 --> 00:02:39.031
I don't play guitar.

00:02:39.031 --> 00:02:40.059
And I um pedal board.

00:02:40.059 --> 00:02:40.892
Thank you.

00:02:40.892 --> 00:02:44.606
And I fell back on it and then
literally the mic somehow hit

00:02:44.606 --> 00:02:47.106
and it was like, it made
the sound from movies like,

00:02:47.106 --> 00:02:48.848
(Screeching Noise)

00:02:48.848 --> 00:02:50.989
like that hole, in an amphitheater filled

00:02:50.989 --> 00:02:54.074
with like 12,000 people
(laughing) and, and it and

00:02:54.074 --> 00:02:55.732
and I just got back up and

00:02:55.732 --> 00:02:57.678
like Mary Katherine Gallagher-ed it

00:02:57.678 --> 00:02:59.685
and was like, yeah, superstar.

00:02:59.685 --> 00:03:02.376
And I just kept going.
- That is my biggest fear.

00:03:02.376 --> 00:03:03.209
- To fall?

00:03:03.209 --> 00:03:04.553
- Oh, don't let it be
because you know what?

00:03:04.553 --> 00:03:06.047
Just get back up and you just
lean into the fact that like

00:03:06.047 --> 00:03:08.290
- But when you're doing
comedy, you're falling alone.

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:09.805
Like at least you have, (laughs) you just-

00:03:09.805 --> 00:03:13.191
- Trust me. Trust me. I
felt alone.(Crowd Laughs)

00:03:13.191 --> 00:03:15.749
I didn't feel like I had a
team of people fall with me.

00:03:15.749 --> 00:03:16.582
- Yeah.

00:03:16.582 --> 00:03:18.059
- On my whole band knows
me too.(Jen and Sam Laugh)

00:03:18.059 --> 00:03:21.036
So they're all laughing like,
everybody's like, oh damn

00:03:21.036 --> 00:03:22.086
she went down.

00:03:22.086 --> 00:03:23.322
You think she's getting up?

00:03:23.322 --> 00:03:24.815
Like it was like it wasn't good.

00:03:24.815 --> 00:03:27.055
It was hilarious, but I
got back up, whatever.

00:03:27.055 --> 00:03:30.078
So now you're in a
movie with an SNL Great.

00:03:30.078 --> 00:03:30.911
This is incredible.

00:03:30.911 --> 00:03:31.744
- Yeah.

00:03:31.744 --> 00:03:33.417
- With Eddie Murphy. So
like, what is this movie

00:03:33.417 --> 00:03:35.389
about? (Crowd Claps) And how
excited and stoked are you?

00:03:35.389 --> 00:03:38.114
- Man, I'm super, super, super excited

00:03:38.114 --> 00:03:39.247
for this movie to come out.

00:03:39.247 --> 00:03:40.080
- [Kelly] Yeah. Yeah. Yeah.

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:41.588
- I can't wait for
people to see it and just

00:03:41.588 --> 00:03:42.883
feel what we were trying to give them.

00:03:42.883 --> 00:03:43.716
- Yeah

00:03:43.716 --> 00:03:45.602
- And I mean it's about
interracial relationship

00:03:45.602 --> 00:03:47.447
and also an interfaith relationship.

00:03:47.447 --> 00:03:50.430
Uh Lauren London and Jonah
Hill are dating. He's Jewish,

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:53.352
she's Muslim and black. And
it's just about all the ups

00:03:53.352 --> 00:03:54.185
and downs of that.

00:03:54.185 --> 00:03:56.396
And how when two people are
just trying to be in love

00:03:56.396 --> 00:03:58.277
there's all these outside
forces that kind of try to

00:03:58.277 --> 00:03:59.110
tear them apart.

00:03:59.110 --> 00:03:59.943
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:59.943 --> 00:04:01.738
- Based on their own preconceived
ideas of what that love is

00:04:01.738 --> 00:04:03.496
- Based on what society
has told us we should.

00:04:03.496 --> 00:04:04.329
- [Sam] Yes.

00:04:04.329 --> 00:04:05.162
- Yeah.

00:04:05.162 --> 00:04:05.995
- [Sam] Exactly.

00:04:05.995 --> 00:04:06.828
- That's interesting.

00:04:06.828 --> 00:04:08.711
I love that you're taking
such a serious heavy topic

00:04:08.711 --> 00:04:09.644
but with humor

00:04:09.644 --> 00:04:10.622
- [Sam] I think that's
the best way to do it.

00:04:10.622 --> 00:04:12.288
- That's the best way. Yeah.
- Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:04:12.288 --> 00:04:13.208
- [Kelly] Yeah

00:04:13.208 --> 00:04:14.083
And then it's like thought-provoking.

00:04:14.083 --> 00:04:15.608
That's my favorite- I
always say this to Joe

00:04:15.608 --> 00:04:16.441
That it's my favorite thing

00:04:16.441 --> 00:04:17.907
to watch something
that's thought-provoking.

00:04:17.907 --> 00:04:19.520
Then afterwards you and your
friends are like discussing.

00:04:19.520 --> 00:04:21.186
- Right. You gotta put a
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:21.186 --> 00:04:22.272
